gories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"OCzo8T-76iJ_QVB2UX5SEQ","review_id":"-Gv0Rb4N_lSf4hO8ddo3oQ","date":"2016-10-26T19:50:42","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9554755687713623,"text_excerpt":"Killer Poboys has converted me into a fan of po'boys. Prior to coming here, I've had a number of disappointing encounters with po'boys. I am so glad that I've tried this place because I definitely didn't know what I was missing! We first heard about this place from our Uber driver who raved about the sandwiches and told us that we have to try it before we leave NOLA. I am glad that she warned us about it being behind the bar because I didn't notice any sign for the place when I walked up to the Erin Rose bar. Pro tip, bring your ID as the you need to be 21 just to step into the place. I wasn't carrying my purse that day, but glad to have the foresight of having my driver's licence in my b..."},{"business_id":"OCzo8T-76iJ_QVB2UX5SEQ","review_id":"O3RaENV9U4MMq939f-mF1A","date":"2014-01-02T02:36:27","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9469265937805176,"text_excerpt":"For $9-12, you will have one of the best Po Boys in NOLA, if you can find the place at the back of Erin Rose. The hosts in the kitchen were very friendly and helpful, and both of our po boys were outstanding. I had the pork belly, and my friend had the barbq lime shrimp. I would be hard pressed to choose between the two, so just go with what you most like or what seems good to you at the time. One of the things I liked about Killer Po Boy is that the sandwiches are not huge, and I did not have an unhealthy or greasy feeling after eating this po boy. The shrimp are grilled, not fried, and the sandwiches were of reasonable size and include carrots or veggies. Grab a drink at the Erin Rose, ..."},{"business_id":"OCzo8T-76iJ_QVB2UX5SEQ","review_id":"jOcPLNlw_kgaObGfXQiXXQ","date":"2013-09-03T22:27:37","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9429251551628113,"text_excerpt":"Quick search on Yelp for Poboys, and my search led me here. Glad to know they're open until midnight as I was hungry and not in the mood for hot dogs or pizza which can be found all along Bourbon. Found inside the Erin Rose bar, be warned this place is cash only. We asked the guy which was his favorite poboy and he goes on to tell us about the special of the day, a lamb sausage poboy. After a vivid description that left my mouth watering, he ended his summary with a, \"Sadly, we're all out for the day.\" .....REALLY?!?! What a tease! In the end after the disappointment of no lamb poboy, I ended up ordering the Dark and Stormy Poboy (pork belly done with a rum ginger glaze, lime slaw, and ga..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"OCzo8T-76iJ_QVB2UX5SEQ","photo_id":"lqQSiU7AX5gEiN_eiaRWpg","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/lqQSiU7AX5gEiN_eiaRWpg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8440903425216675},{"business_id":"OCzo8T-76iJ_QVB2UX5SEQ","photo_id":"ls0X0-BrabHiS2hr7q1Wqw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/ls0X0-BrabHiS2hr7q1Wqw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8323917984962463},{"business_id":"OCzo8T-76iJ_QVB2UX5SEQ","photo_id":"Bw52ko1d0_lxWl88DgJHFA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Bw52ko1d0_lxWl88DgJHFA.j